+## RequestBodyLimitMiddleware
+
+Buffers HTTP request bodies before calling the application and rejects bodies
+larger than `max_bytes` with a plain-text 413 response containing exactly
+`Request body too large`. It counts received bytes regardless of `Content-Length`
+and stops receiving at the first chunk that exceeds the limit.
+
+```python
+from starlette.applications import Starlette
+from starlette.middleware import Middleware
+from starlette.middleware.body_limit import RequestBodyLimitMiddleware
+
+app = Starlette(
+    routes=...,
+    middleware=[Middleware(RequestBodyLimitMiddleware, max_bytes=1024 * 1024)],
+)
+```
+
+`max_bytes` must be `None` or a non-negative integer, excluding booleans. Invalid
+limits raise `ValueError` at construction. `None` disables buffering and the limit.
+Accepted bodies are replayed to the application, so request body and JSON helpers
+work normally. Subsequent receives are delegated to the original stream.
+WebSocket and lifespan scopes pass through without buffering.
+
